    {
      "id": "claim_eb4234b9788e40caa5fb9c17cbd04fd9",
      "statement": "public/terms.html and public/privacy.html are static HTML files served from public/ with no build step or framework. They are static rather than app routes on purpose: a blocked user has no session, so anything routed through the app would sit behind the gate they are trying to read their way out of. A file in public/ is served to anyone, in any state, and opens in a new tab without booting the app.",
      "evidence": [
