    {
      "id": "claim_3c380b0d49f44281a76e87deb179b80b",
      "statement": "The userConsentsSchema defines latestConsents (with tos, pp, and acceptedAt as a BSON date) and consents (the history array) on the user document. Neither field is in required because registration does not write them. Two JWT claims — latestConsents/tos and latestConsents/pp — carry the versions in the token so the Guards rule can read them without a database round-trip; if either claim is missing, every authenticated user is blocked permanently.",
